<<set $idolCracked to false>><<set $vaultPeace to false>>
<<set $crawling to false>><<set $light to 0>><<set $dread to 0>><<set $prov to 0>><<set $flasks to 0>><<set $salt to 0>>
<<set $stir to 0>><<set $nextHunt to 6>><<set $moves to 0>><<set $hunt to false>><<set $huntDest to "">>
<<set $depth to 1>><<set $seen to {}>><<set $survivor to false>><<set $knowsName to false>><<set $journal to false>><<set $chalk to false>>
<<set $packFrom to "">><<set $campAt to "">><<set $deepMethod to "">><<set $foe to null>>
<<set $party to []>><<set $trust to {}>><<set $talked to {}>><<set $campTalk to {}>>
<<set $talkNpc to "">><<set $talkBack to "">><<set $topicText to []>><<set $topicNote to "">>
<<set $partyBack to "">><<set $partyTalkId to "">><<set $partyTalkText to []>><<set $partyTalkNote to "">>
<<set $recruitHub to "">><<set $recruitBack to "">><<set $joinMsg to "">><<set $joinBack to "">>
<<set $partyGuard to 0>><<set $partyBoost to 0>><<set $leftNames to []>><<set $lastCampCost to 1>>
<<set $maeveDeal to false>><<set $wolfWarn to false>><<set $holdMap to false>><<set $sabHelp to false>>
<<set $hintLedger to false>><<set $hintCistern to false>><<set $hintSpore to false>><<set $hintSilk to false>>
<<set $kessrickLore to false>><<set $vessWants to false>><<set $gateHint to false>><<set $saltDeal to false>>

:: StoryCaption
<<if $final>>
<b><<= $name>></b><br>
<<= $race>> <<= $class>><br>
Stamina <<= $hp>>/<<= $maxhp>> &middot; Guard <<= $guard>><br>
Crowns <<= $gold>> &middot; Draughts <<= $potions>><br>
Sparks <<= $sparks>><<if $race is "Drakeblood">> &middot; Breath <<= $breath>><</if>>
<<if $party.length>><br>Party: <<= $party.map(function (i) { return setup.companions[i].short; }).join(", ")>><</if>>
<<if $crawling>>
<br>Light <<= $light>> &middot; Dread <<= $dread>>/10<br>
Provisions <<= $prov>> &middot; Flasks <<= $flasks>><br>
<<set _f to Math.max(0, Math.min(6, 6 - ($nextHunt - $stir)))>>
The Deep stirs: <<= "▮".repeat(_f) + "▯".repeat(6 - _f)>>
<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Start
<div class="title-block">
<h1>Tales of the Western Reach</h1>
<p><em>Three fantasy adventures for a single hero</em></p>
</div>

The Western Reach in autumn: cold rain on the King's Road, woodsmoke on the wind, and rumors of trouble in the river town of Brackenford. You are about to become part of one of those rumors.

First, you must decide who you are.

[[Create your character|Name]]

:: Name
<h2>Your name</h2>
What are you called, traveler?

<<textbox "$name" "Adventurer" "Race" autofocus>>

[[Continue|Race]]

:: Race
<h2>Choose your lineage</h2>
<<for _k, _r range setup.races>>
<<capture _k>>
<div class="opt"><<link _k>><<set $race to _k>><<goto "Class">><</link>> - <em><<= _r.summary>></em><br><small><<= _r.traits>></small></div>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

:: Class
<h2>Choose your calling</h2>
<<for _k, _c range setup.classes>>
<<capture _k>>
<div class="opt"><<link _k>><<set $class to _k>><<goto "Background">><</link>> - <em><<= _c.summary>></em><br><small>Attacks with <<= setup.attributeNames[_c.atk]>> &middot; Armor <<= _c.armor>> &middot; Trained: <<= _c.skills.join(", ")>> &middot; Signature feat: <b><<= _c.feat>></b> (<<= _c.featDesc>>)</small></div>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

:: Background
<h2>Choose your past</h2>
<<for _k, _b range setup.backgrounds>>
<<capture _k>>
<div class="opt"><<link _k>><<set $bg to _k>><<goto "ExtraSkill">><</link>> - <em><<= _b.summary>></em><br><small>Trained: <<= _b.skills.join(", ")>> &middot; Starting crowns: <<= _b.gold>></small></div>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

:: ExtraSkill
<h2>One more talent</h2>
Every adventurer has a knack all their own. Pick one extra knack to be trained in. Trained knacks add 2 dice to your pool.

<div class="actions">
<<for _s range ["Perception", "Investigation", "Persuasion", "Discernment", "Stealth", "Acrobatics"]>>
<<capture _s>>
<<link _s>><<set $extraSkill to _s>><<set $base to {vig:1, fin:1, wit:1, pre:1}>><<set $points to 6>><<goto "Abilities">><</link>>
<</capture>>
<</for>>
</div>

:: Abilities
<h2>Attributes</h2>
Four Attributes describe what you are like. Each starts at 1, and its rating is the number of dice you roll. You have <b><<= $points>></b> points left to spend (no Attribute above 4 before lineage bonuses).

<<for _a range setup.attributes>>
<<capture _a>>
<div class="abrow"><span class="ablabel"><<= setup.attributeNames[_a]>></span><<link "-">><<run setup.bump(_a, -1)>><<goto "Abilities">><</link>> <b class="abval"><<= $base[_a]>></b> <<link "+">><<run setup.bump(_a, 1)>><<goto "Abilities">><</link>><span class="abnote"><<= setup.attributeDesc[_a]>><<if setup.races[$race].bonus[_a]>> &middot; +<<= setup.races[$race].bonus[_a]>> from lineage = <b><<= Math.min(5, $base[_a] + setup.races[$race].bonus[_a])>></b><</if>></span></div>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

<div class="actions">
<<link `"Use the recommended " + $class + " build"`>><<run setup.applyRec()>><<goto "Abilities">><</link>>
<<link "Finish character">><<run setup.finalize()>><<goto "Sheet">><</link>>
</div>

:: Sheet
<h2><<= $name>></h2>
<<= $race>> <<= $class>>, <<= $bg>>

<table class="sheet">
<tr><<for _a range setup.attributes>><th><<= setup.attributeNames[_a]>></th><</for>></tr>
<tr><<for _a range setup.attributes>><td><<= $final[_a]>> dice</td><</for>></tr>
</table>

<b>Stamina</b> <<= $maxhp>> &middot; <b>Guard</b> <<= $guard>> &middot; <b>Sparks</b> <<= $sparks>> &middot; <b>Crowns</b> <<= $gold>>

<b>Trained knacks (+2 dice):</b> <<= $skills.join(", ")>>

<b>Gear:</b> <<= $inv.join(", ")>>, 2 healing draughts

<b>Lineage:</b> <<= setup.races[$race].traits>>

<b>Signature feat (costs 1 Spark):</b> <<= setup.classes[$class].feat>>, <<= setup.classes[$class].featDesc>>

<h3>How the rules work</h3>
To attempt something risky, roll a pool of six-sided dice equal to the relevant Attribute, plus 2 if you are Trained in the knack. Add one <b>Fate die</b>. Every die showing 4 or higher is a <b>hit</b>. A Fate 6 counts as two hits, but a Fate 1 cancels one. Harder tasks need more hits.

In a fight, your hits beyond the foe's <b>Guard</b> become damage. Each round, choose a stance: <b>Strike</b>, <b>Press</b> (more dice, but lower Guard), <b>Brace</b> (higher Guard and a little healing), or spend a <b>Spark</b> on your calling's feat.

Choose your adventure:

[[The Silent Bell of Brackenford (a short story-driven quest)|Prologue]]
[[The Weeping Rift (open-ended: explore a frontier ravine at your own pace)|RiftIntro]]
[[The Lampless Deep (a horror dungeon crawl: manage Light, Dread and supplies)|DeepIntro]]

[[Start over|Name]]

:: Prologue
The rain has followed you for three days along the King's Road. Toward dusk, you crest a rise and find a merchant wagon on its side in the mud, its canvas torn, its horses gone.

A woman sits against a wheel, clutching her arm. Her cart bells, the little brass ones every caravan hangs from its harness, have all been cut away.

"Thank the gods," she gasps. "Maeve Thornbrook, of Thornbrook & Daughters. Robed folk came out of the trees. They didn't say a word, they only hummed. They took my guards and every bell on the wagons, and left me alive to carry a warning."

[[Kneel beside her|Wagon]]

:: Wagon
Maeve watches you with tired, hopeful eyes. The wreck and the road are still full of secrets.

<<if not $tended>>[[Tend Maeve's wounds|WagonTend]]<<else>><span class="dim">You have tended Maeve's wounds.</span><</if>>
<<if not $tracked>>[[Study the tracks around the wagon|WagonTracks]]<<else>><span class="dim">You have studied the tracks.</span><</if>>

[[Help Maeve to Brackenford|Brackenford]]
<<talklink "maeve" "Talk with Maeve">>

:: WagonTend
<<chk "wit" "Medicine" 1>>
<<set $tended to true>>
<<if _ok>>
You clean and bind the wound with steady hands. Maeve sighs in relief. "You have a healer's touch. Take this, my last good vial."
<<set $potions++>>
You gain a healing draught.
<<else>>
Your bandaging is clumsy, and Maeve winces. She thanks you anyway, but you fear the wound will trouble her.
<</if>>

[[Back to the wagon|Wagon]]

:: WagonTracks
<<chk "wit" "Perception" 2>>
<<set $tracked to true>>
<<if _ok>>
Among the churned mud you find bare footprints, dozens of them, all heading the same way: north-east, toward the old Dunvar ruins in the hills. At the edge of the road, someone scratched a sigil into a milestone: three rings, one inside another, like ripples from a bell.
<<set $clues++>>
<<else>>
The rain has turned the ground to soup. You find nothing but mud and hoofprints, and the nagging feeling that you missed something.
<</if>>

[[Back to the wagon|Wagon]]

:: Brackenford
Brackenford sits on the banks of the River Sable, all timber walls, river mist, and lantern light. Maeve is passed to a healer's care. The guards at the gate look worried.

It takes you a moment to notice why the town feels wrong. There are no bells. No temple bell ringing the evening hour, no harness bells on the market carts. Even the river ferry's brass bell has been silenced.

Where will you go?

[[The Temple of First Light|Temple]]
[[The Gilded Heron (an inn)|Inn]]
[[The market|Market]]
[[The docks|Docks]]
<<if $clues gte 2>>
[[Leave for Dunvar Hold|Journey]]
<<else>>
<span class="dim">(You do not yet know enough to know where to look. Ask around.)</span>
<</if>>
<<talklink "maeve" "Visit Maeve at the healer's">>
<<partylink>>

:: Temple
Brother Alden, a gaunt priest with ink-stained fingers, stands in the bell tower's shadow, staring at an empty frame where the great bell once hung.

"Two nights ago it rang matins as always. By dawn it was gone. No rope cut, no door forced, and no one heard a thing."

<<if not $sawTemple>>
<<set $sawTemple to true>>
<<if $class is "Vowed" or $bg is "Temple-raised">>
He notices your faith and brightens. "A fellow servant! Take this, a blessing in a bottle, from our stores."
<<set $potions++>>
You gain a healing draught.
<</if>>
<<chk "wit" "Religion" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You recognize the chalk sigil scrawled inside the tower: three rings within rings. "The Hollow Choir," you murmur. A heretic sect that believed a great bell could carry a voice to the gods, and was cast out from Brackenford a century ago.
<<set $clues++>>
<<else>>
You study the strange rings chalked on the stones, but their meaning slips away from you.
<</if>>
<<else>>
He has nothing more to tell you, but he thanks you for caring.
<</if>>

[[Return to town|Brackenford]]
<<talklink "alden" "Talk with Brother Alden">>

:: Inn
The Gilded Heron is warm, crowded, and unusually quiet. A hush hangs over the drinkers, as if everyone were listening for a sound that never comes.

<<if not $sawTomas>>[[Talk to Tomas, the stablehand|InnTomas]]<<else>><span class="dim">You have spoken with Tomas.</span><</if>>
[[Rent a bed and rest (3 crowns)|InnRest]]
[[Return to town|Brackenford]]
<<recruitlink "bell">>
<<partylink>>

:: InnTomas
Tomas, a lanky youth with worried eyes, keeps glancing at the door. He clearly knows something.

[[Buy him a hot meal (2 crowns)|InnTomasBuy]]
[[Coax the story out of him|InnTomasTalk]]
[[Leave him be|Inn]]
<<talklink "tomas" "Just chat with Tomas">>

:: InnTomasBuy
<<if $gold gte 2>>
<<set $gold -= 2>><<set $sawTomas to true>><<set $clues++>>
Tomas wolfs down the stew. "Two nights ago I was out with the horses and I saw them. Robed folk on the north road, humming, carrying a big black bell wrapped in sackcloth. They went toward Dunvar Hold, the old dwarven ruin in the hills. It's a week's walk by road, or a day by river if Old Corvin will take you."
<<else>>
You don't have enough gold.
<</if>>

[[Back|Inn]]

:: InnTomasTalk
<<chk "pre" "Persuasion" 1>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $sawTomas to true>><<set $clues++>>
Tomas leans in and whispers what he saw: robed figures on the north road, carrying a great black bell toward Dunvar Hold, the old dwarven ruin in the hills. "Old Corvin the boatman can get you there faster than the road."
<<else>>
Tomas clams up. "Ain't nothing to tell, stranger." You'll need a better approach, or a better meal.
<</if>>

[[Back|Inn]]

:: InnRest
<<if $gold gte 3>>
<<set $gold -= 3>><<run setup.rest()>>
You sleep soundly. When you wake, you are fully rested. Stamina and Sparks are restored.
<<else>>
You can't afford a bed.
<</if>>

[[Back|Inn]]

:: Market
The market is half empty. Stalls stand with awnings drawn and shopkeepers speak in low voices.

<<set _pr to ($maeveDeal ? 6 : 8)>>
<<if $gold gte _pr>>
<<link `"Buy a healing draught (" + _pr + " crowns)"`>><<set $gold -= _pr>><<set $potions++>><<goto "Market">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">Healing draught: <<= _pr>> crowns (you can't afford one).</span>
<</if>>

<<if not $lantern>>
<<if $gold gte 2>>
<<link "Buy a hooded lantern and oil (2 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 2>><<set $lantern to true>><<goto "Market">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">Lantern and oil: 2 crowns.</span>
<</if>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">You already carry a lantern.</span>
<</if>>

You have <<= $gold>> crowns.

[[Return to town|Brackenford]]

:: Docks
Old Corvin, a barge-master with a face like tanned leather, is mending nets on the quay. His ferry bell is missing too.

<<if not $sawDocks>>
<<set $sawDocks to true>>
"Aye, I know Dunvar Hold. My grandfather ran salvage there when the dwarves still held it. There's an old landing on the river, a day upstream. I'll take you, if you don't mind the current."
<<set $shortcut to true>><<set $clues++>>
<<else>>
"Ready when you are, friend. Just say the word."
<</if>>

[[Return to town|Brackenford]]
<<talklink "corvin" "Talk with Old Corvin">>

:: Journey
<<set $checkpoint to "Journey">>
Dunvar Hold lies in the hills north-east of town, a ruined dwarven hall swallowed by the wild. You can reach it two ways.

[[Follow the old road on foot|WolfAmbush]]
<<if $shortcut>>[[Take Old Corvin's boat upriver|RiverRoute]]<</if>>

:: RiverRoute
Old Corvin poles his flat barge upriver through the dawn mist, muttering a prayer with no bell to ring it.

<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You lend your strength at the pole and the barge glides through the rapids. Corvin nods gruffly. "You've a river's patience."
<<else>>
The current slams the barge against a rock. You're thrown against the gunwale and lose a few Stamina.
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 4))>>
<</if>>

By evening, the ruined landing of Dunvar Hold looms ahead.

[[Approach the gates|HoldGate]]

:: WolfAmbush
<<set $checkpoint to "WolfAmbush">>
The road climbs into grey hills. You've walked half a day when something in the bracken snarls. A gaunt dire wolf pads out onto the road, ribs showing, eyes ringed with a strange pale light.

You can't tell if it's hunting, or has been driven here by whatever is calling from the hold.

<<link "Draw steel and fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Starving Wolf", hp:($wolfWarn ? 8 : 11), guard:1, pool:4, dmg:2, loot:4, win:"HoldGate"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: Combat
<<if $fight.hp lte 0>>
<<goto "Victory">>
<<elseif $hp lte 0>>
<<goto "Defeat">>
<<else>>
<div class="enemy"><b><<= $fight.name>></b> &middot; Stamina <<= Math.max(0, $fight.hp)>>/<<= $fight.max>> &middot; Guard <<= $fight.guard>> &middot; Attacks with <<= $fight.pool>> dice</div>
<<if $party.length>><div class="dim">Fighting beside you: <<= $party.map(function (i) { return setup.companions[i].short; }).join(", ")>></div><</if>>
<div class="log"><<for _l range $fight.log>><p><<= _l>></p><</for>></div>
<div class="actions">
<<link `"Strike (" + setup.classes[$class].weapon + ")"`>><<run setup.act("strike")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<link "Press (+2 dice, -1 Guard)">><<run setup.act("press")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<link "Brace (+2 Guard, recover 1)">><<run setup.act("brace")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<if $sparks gt 0>>
<<link `setup.classes[$class].feat + " (1 Spark, " + $sparks + " left)"`>><<run setup.act("feat")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<<else>><span class="dim">[<<= setup.classes[$class].feat>>: no Sparks]</span><</if>>
<<if $race is "Drakeblood" and $breath gt 0>>
<<link "Breath Weapon">><<run setup.act("breath")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>
<<if $potions gt 0>>
<<link `"Drink a healing draught (" + $potions + " left)"`>><<run setup.act("potion")>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>
</div>
<</if>>

:: Victory
<<for _l range $fight.log>><p><<= _l>></p><</for>>
<p><b>The <<= $fight.name>> is defeated!</b></p>
<<set _bv to setup.banter("victory")>><<if _bv>><p><i><<= _bv>></i></p><</if>>
<<if $fight.loot gt 0>>
<<set $gold += $fight.loot>>
You find <<= $fight.loot>> crowns among its remains.
<</if>>

<<link "Continue">><<goto $fight.win>><</link>>

:: Defeat
<<if $crawling>>
The world goes dark. You wake in the last place you rested, cold, hurt, and shaken. Whatever dragged you back took some of your supplies and a piece of your nerve.
<<set $hp to Math.max(1, Math.floor($maxhp / 2))>>
<<run setup.crawlSetback()>>
<<set $fight to null>>
<b>-1 Provision, -2 Light, +2 Dread.</b>
<<else>>
The world goes dark. You awaken later, bruised, robbed of a few coins, but alive. Something, or someone, dragged you clear.

<<set $hp to Math.max(1, Math.floor($maxhp / 2))>>
<<set $gold to Math.max(0, $gold - 5)>>
<<set $fight to null>>
<</if>>

<<link "Rise and try again">><<goto $checkpoint>><</link>>

:: HoldGate
<<set $checkpoint to "HoldGate">>
Dunvar Hold rises from the hillside, a great ruined gate of dwarven stone, half buried in moss and time. From inside comes a low, wordless hum that rattles your teeth and makes your bones ache.

The great doors stand ajar. Beyond is darkness.

[[Slip inside|HallOfEchoes]]

:: HallOfEchoes
The gate opens onto a long hall of carved pillars. The hum is stronger here, and it echoes strangely, as if every stone were a throat.

<<if setup.races[$race].dark or $lantern>>
<<if setup.races[$race].dark>>Your nightsight picks out the hall in shades of grey.<<else>>Your lantern throws warm light across the pillars.<</if>>
<<else>>
You have no light at all. You barely take three steps before you bark your shin on a fallen column and lose some Stamina.
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 4))>>
<</if>>

Ahead, the floor is a checkerboard of stone plates, some worn, some new. Beyond them, a door glows faintly.

How do you cross?

<<link "Study the plates (Investigation)">><<set $hallMethod to "Investigation">><<goto "HallSolve">><</link>>
<<link "Read the dwarven runes on the pillars (History)">><<set $hallMethod to "History">><<goto "HallSolve">><</link>>
<<link "Leap across, plate to plate (Acrobatics)">><<set $hallMethod to "Acrobatics">><<goto "HallSolve">><</link>>

:: HallSolve
<<if $hallMethod is "Investigation">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 2 - ($holdMap ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "wit" "Investigation" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You notice that only some plates are worn smooth by centuries of dwarven boots. The others are bright and new, and wired to something below. You step carefully on the worn ones.<</if>>
<<elseif $hallMethod is "History">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 2 - ($holdMap ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "wit" "History" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You read the runes: "Where stone is worn, the wise may walk." You match them to the plates and cross safely.<</if>>
<<else>>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 3 - ($holdMap ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "fin" "Acrobatics" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You vault from plate to plate, barely touching each one. Nothing triggers.<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if not _ok>>
Your foot lands on the wrong plate. Click. A volley of poisoned darts hisses out of the pillars!
<<set _d to random(1, 6)>>
<<if $race is "Dwarf">><<set _d to Math.ceil(_d / 2)>>Your dwarven constitution shrugs off some of the poison.<</if>>
You take <<= _d>> damage.
<<run setup.hurt(_d)>>
<</if>>

You reach the glowing door at the far end of the hall.

[[Open it|Chapel]]

:: Chapel
<<set $checkpoint to "Chapel">>
Beyond the door lies a vaulted chapel, once a dwarven shrine to a smith-god. Now, two robed figures stand before an altar, humming in perfect unison. Their mouths do not move. The sound comes from somewhere else.

Behind them, a side door leads deeper into the hold. On a hook near you hangs a spare grey robe.

<<link "Attack them head-on!">><<goto "ChapelFight">><</link>>
<<link "Sneak along the wall (Stealth)">><<goto "ChapelSneak">><</link>>
<<link "Put on the robe and walk past (Deception)">><<goto "ChapelDisguise">><</link>>

:: ChapelSneak
<<chk "fin" "Stealth" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $sneaked to true>>
You slip along the shadows of the wall, holding your breath. The Acolytes never turn. You reach the side door and ease it open.

[[Go through|Cells]]
<<else>>
A boot scrapes on stone. The humming stops. Two heads turn as one.

[[Fight!|ChapelFight]]
<</if>>

:: ChapelDisguise
<<chk "pre" "Deception" 3>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $sneaked to true>>
You pull the robe over your head, adopt a slow, swaying gait, and hum tunelessly. One Acolyte tilts its head at you, then goes back to its song. You slip through the side door.

[[Go through|Cells]]
<<else>>
Your hum is off-key. The Acolytes stop and stare. One slowly points a finger at you.

[[Fight!|ChapelFight]]
<</if>>

:: ChapelFight
<<set $checkpoint to "Chapel">>
The Choir Acolytes turn together, and the hum becomes a shriek. Their eyes are hollow, their mouths sewn shut.

<<link "Steel yourself and fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Choir Acolytes", hp:16, guard:1, pool:4, dmg:2, loot:6, win:"Cells"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: Cells
<<set $checkpoint to "Cells">>
Beyond the chapel, iron-barred cells line a low tunnel. In the last cell, a broad-shouldered man in a caravan guard's tabard sits with his head in his hands.

"Sergeant Bram Holloway," he croaks. "Thornbrook's guard. The rest are... I can't hear them anymore. They took our voices, friend. Right out of our throats."

<<if not $bram>>
You break the lock. Bram climbs to his feet, retrieves a discarded sword, and pledges to stand beside you.
<<set $bram to true>>
He binds your wounds with a healer's kit.
<<run setup.heal(Math.ceil(($maxhp - $hp) / 2))>>
<</if>>

"The Choirmaster keeps the Hollow Bell in the chamber below," Bram whispers. "It's the source of the hum. He's been feeding it voices."

[[Descend to the Bell Chamber|BellChamber]]
<<talklink "bram" "Talk with Bram">>
<<if $party.indexOf("bram") lt 0>><<joinlink "bram" "Ask Bram to fight beside you" "Cells">><<else>><span class="dim">Bram is with you.</span><</if>>

:: BellChamber
<<set $checkpoint to "BellChamber">>
The stairs open onto a cavernous shrine. At its heart hangs the Hollow Bell, black as a pit, taller than a man. It hums without being struck, and each pulse of sound makes your chest ache.

Beneath it stands a tall, thin man in tattered priest's robes. He turns as you enter. His face is calm, and his eyes are wet with tears.

"Ah," says Choirmaster Veyle, and his voice is a whisper, a ruin. "More voices."

<<if $bram>>Sergeant Bram stands at your shoulder, sword drawn, jaw clenched.<</if>>

How do you face him?

<<if not $gotDiscernment>>
<<link "Read his face (Discernment)">><<goto "BossDiscernment">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">You understand his grief.</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Speak to him (Persuasion)">><<goto "BossParley">><</link>>
<<if not $sabotaged>>
<<link "Sabotage the bell with Occult">><<set $sabMethod to "Occult">><<goto "BossSabotage">><</link>>
<<link "Sabotage the bell with Religion">><<set $sabMethod to "Religion">><<goto "BossSabotage">><</link>>
<<link "Topple the bell by force (Athletics)">><<set $sabMethod to "Athletics">><<goto "BossSabotage">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The bell's hum is fractured and weak.</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Attack the Choirmaster!">><<goto "BossFight">><</link>>
<<talklink "veyle" "Speak with Veyle before you decide">>

:: BossDiscernment
<<chk "wit" "Discernment" 2>>
<<set $gotDiscernment to true>>
<<if _ok>>
You see it plainly. Veyle was once a bell-warden of this hold's shrine. He lost his own voice to some old grief, and the bell offered him a way to hear a voice again, even if it wasn't his own. He isn't cruel. He is a lonely, broken man who cannot stop.
<<else>>
His face is a mask of calm. You sense only sorrow, deep and old, but not its cause.
<</if>>

[[Return|BellChamber]]

:: BossParley
<<if $gotDiscernment>><<set _dc to 2>><<else>><<set _dc to 4>><</if>>
<<chk "pre" "Persuasion" _dc>>
<<if _ok>>
You lower your weapon and speak: not of justice, but of what he has lost, and what he is doing to others. Veyle's shoulders slump. The hum stutters.

[[Continue|EndPeace]]
<<else>>
Veyle listens, then shakes his head sadly. "Kind words, but the Choir is never silent. Please forgive me."

The Hollow Bell surges.

[[Defend yourself!|BossFight]]
<</if>>

:: BossSabotage
<<if $sabMethod is "Occult">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 2 - ($sabHelp ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "wit" "Occult" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You trace the bell's runes. They are a weave of resonance and binding. One sharp counter-note unravels the knot at its core.<</if>>
<<elseif $sabMethod is "Religion">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 2 - ($sabHelp ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "wit" "Religion" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You recall the old rites for silencing a tainted bell. You speak the words of quieting, and the metal shudders.<</if>>
<<else>>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 3 - ($sabHelp ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "vig" "Athletics" _n>>
<<if _ok>>You wedge your shoulder against the great bell and heave. Ancient chains groan, and it slips its mount, crashing against the wall.<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if _ok>>
<<set $sabotaged to true>>
A great crack runs through the Hollow Bell. Its hum warbles, cracks, and fades to a dull throb. Veyle cries out and staggers.

"What have you done?"

[[Return|BellChamber]]
<<else>>
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 6))>>
The bell answers with a shriek that shakes your skull. You lose a few Stamina as Veyle draws himself up.

[[Face him|BossFight]]
<</if>>

:: BossFight
<<set $checkpoint to "BellChamber">>
<<set $bossDef to {name:"Choirmaster Veyle", hp:26, guard:2, pool:5, dmg:2, loot:0, win:"EndShatter"}>>
<<if $sabotaged>><<set $bossDef.hp to 18>><<set $bossDef.guard to 1>><<set $bossDef.pool to 4>><</if>>
<<if $bram>><<set $bossDef.pool to $bossDef.pool - 1>><</if>>

Veyle raises his hands. The Hollow Bell resonates, and the air itself vibrates with his stolen voices.

<<if $sabotaged>>The cracked bell can barely amplify him. He seems weakened.<</if>>
<<if $bram>>Sergeant Bram charges in beside you, drawing Veyle's attention.<</if>>

<<link "Fight the Choirmaster!">><<run setup.startFight($bossDef)>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: EndPeace
Choirmaster Veyle lets his hands fall. "I only wanted... to hear again."

He steps to the bell and lays a trembling palm on it. With a sound like a sigh, the Hollow Bell cracks from crown to lip, and a thousand stolen voices rush out through the stone. In the cells above, the captured guards gasp, weep, laugh. Bram lets out a roar that shakes the cavern.

Veyle sinks to his knees, and after a long moment, he speaks in a small, cracked, but wholly his own voice. "Thank you."

[[Return to Brackenford|TheEnd]]

:: EndShatter
Choirmaster Veyle falls beside the Hollow Bell. As his last breath leaves him, the black bell shatters, and a thousand stolen voices burst out through the stone in a rush like a thunderclap.

<<if $sabotaged>>The bell was already broken, and now it is only scrap and silence.<</if>>

In the cells above, the captured guards gasp, weep, laugh. <<if $bram>>Bram lets out a roar that shakes the cavern.<</if>> The hum is gone at last.

[[Return to Brackenford|TheEnd]]

:: TheEnd
You return to Brackenford at dawn with the rescued caravan guards in tow. At the temple, Brother Alden hangs a small brass bell from the empty tower frame, one salvaged from Maeve's wrecked wagon, and gives it a tug.

Ding.

Every bell in Brackenford answers. The ferry, the harness bells, the temple, all ringing at once, as if the town were remembering how to sing. Maeve Thornbrook weeps in the market square. Old Corvin takes off his cap.

The people of Brackenford cheer your name, <<= $name>>.

<<set $gold += 50>>
Maeve presses a purse into your hands: 50 crowns, and a promise that Thornbrook & Daughters will always carry your goods for free.

<<for _be range setup.banterAll("end")>><p><i><<= _be>></i></p><</for>>
<h2>The End</h2>
<p><em><<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>>. Stamina <<= $hp>>/<<= $maxhp>>, <<= $gold>> crowns.</em></p>

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: RiftIntro
The frontier road ends at Thornwatch Keep, a squat ring of grey towers on a windswept ridge, the last stone wall between the Western Reach's farmland and the wild hills.

Beyond the keep, the land splits open. The Weeping Rift is a mile-long ravine, its walls pocked with cave mouths and slick with seeping water. For decades it was empty. Now, patrols that ride into it do not ride out. Herders swear the caves glow at night, and the wind carries howls, chanting, and something like distant hammering.

The keep's Warden-Captain is paying coin to anyone who will look into it.

[[Enter the keep|RiftKeep]]

:: RiftKeep
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftKeep">>
Thornwatch Keep bustles with the wary energy of a place under quiet siege. Soldiers drill in the yard, traders haggle over the price of lamp oil, and every eye keeps drifting toward the ravine.

<<if $sigils gt 0>>You carry <<= $sigils>> of the Rift's four ash-black sigil stones.<</if>>

[[Warden-Captain Marrow's hall|RiftCaptain]]
[[The Traders' Yard|RiftShop]]
[[The Broken Shield (tavern)|RiftTavern]]
[[Ride out to the Weeping Rift|RiftRavine]]
<<partylink>>

:: RiftCaptain
Warden-Captain Isolde Marrow, a weathered woman with a scar across her jaw, studies a map with four cave mouths circled in red.

<<if not $metCaptain>>
<<set $metCaptain to true>>
"Something in the Rift is stirring the monsters up. I count four lairs that matter. Clear them, or make peace with them, I don't care which. Whatever you find, bring back anything that looks like ash-black stone. My scouts say these 'sigils' are keys to something buried at the ravine's end."

She hands you a sealed flask and a purse. "For your trouble. Come back alive."
<<set $potions++>><<set $gold += 10>>
You gain a healing draught and 10 crowns.
<<else>>
"Back already? Tell me what you've found."
<</if>>

<<if $sigils gte 3>>
She turns a sigil in her fingers. "Three of them fit the pattern of the vault door. The Rift's heart is open to you. Whoever is behind this, end it."
<<elseif $sigils gt 0>>
"Good work. Keep looking. I think three sigils will unlock the vault door at the ravine's end."
<</if>>

[[Leave|RiftKeep]]
<<talklink "marrow" "Talk with the Warden-Captain">>

:: RiftTavern
The Broken Shield is loud and low-ceilinged. Innkeeper Hessa Brindle wipes a mug and listens to everything.

Rumors circulating tonight:
<<if not $rift.spore>>* Villagers went missing near the glowing cave. They came back different, and didn't know their own names.<</if>>
<<if not $rift.ledger>>* A deserter company calling itself the Crimson Ledger has fortified a cave and taxes anyone who passes.<</if>>
<<if not $rift.silk>>* Something with too many legs has been dragging livestock into a cave hung with silk.<</if>>
<<if not $rift.cistern>>* An old hag lives in the flooded cistern under the cliff. She trades favors, for a price.<</if>>

<<if $gold gte 3>>
<<link "Rent a bed and rest (3 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 3>><<run setup.rest()>><<goto "RiftTavern">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">A bed costs 3 crowns.</span>
<</if>>

[[Leave|RiftKeep]]
<<talklink "hessa" "Talk with Hessa">>
<<recruitlink "rift">>
<<partylink>>

:: RiftShop
The Traders' Yard smells of tar and rope. You have <<= $gold>> crowns.

<<if $gold gte 8>><<link "Healing draught (8 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 8>><<set $potions++>><<goto "RiftShop">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Healing draught: 8 crowns.</span><</if>>
<<if not $lantern>><<if $gold gte 2>><<link "Hooded lantern and oil (2 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 2>><<set $lantern to true>><<goto "RiftShop">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Lantern and oil: 2 crowns.</span><</if>><<else>><span class="dim">You carry a lantern.</span><</if>>
<<if not $antitoxin>><<if $gold gte 5>><<link "Antitoxin vial (5 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 5>><<set $antitoxin to true>><<goto "RiftShop">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Antitoxin vial: 5 crowns.</span><</if>><<else>><span class="dim">You carry an antitoxin vial.</span><</if>>

[[Leave|RiftKeep]]

:: RiftRavine
The Weeping Rift yawns before you. Water seeps down its walls in thin, glittering threads, and the wind carries a low, uneasy murmur. Four cave mouths dominate the ravine.

<<if not $rift.spore>>[[The green glow: the Sporegrotto|RiftSpore]]<<else>><span class="dim">The Sporegrotto is quiet.</span><</if>>
<<if not $rift.ledger>>[[The walled cave with banners: the Crimson Ledger|RiftLedger]]<<else>><span class="dim">The Crimson Ledger's camp is empty.</span><</if>>
<<if not $rift.silk>>[[The silk-hung cave: the Silk Galleries|RiftSilk]]<<else>><span class="dim">The Silk Galleries are cold.</span><</if>>
<<if not $rift.cistern>>[[The flooded cave: the Brine Cistern|RiftCistern]]<<else>><span class="dim">The Brine Cistern is still.</span><</if>>

<<if $sigils gte 3>>
[[The sealed vault at the ravine's end|RiftVault]]
<<else>>
<span class="dim">At the ravine's far end, a door of ash-black stone waits. It needs three sigils.</span>
<</if>>

[[Return to the keep|RiftKeep]]

:: RiftSpore
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftSpore">><<set $lair to "spore">>
The cave mouth pulses with pale green light. Inside, hollow-eyed figures sway in a carpet of luminous fungus, herders and villagers, their skin dusted with spores, their mouths bloomed with pale caps. They do not speak. They do not seem to blink.

Something old and hungry is growing here, and it has a sigil buried at its core.

<<link "Cover your face and cut through the spores (Survival)">><<set $lairMethod to "Survival">><<goto "RiftSporeResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Study the fungus for a weakness (Medicine)">><<set $lairMethod to "Medicine">><<goto "RiftSporeResolve">><</link>>
<<if $lantern>><<link "Burn the growth with lantern oil">><<set $lairMethod to "Fire">><<goto "RiftSporeResolve">><</link>><</if>>

:: RiftSporeResolve
<<if $lairMethod is "Survival">>
<<chk "wit" "Survival" 2>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Medicine">>
<<chk "wit" "Medicine" 2>>
<<else>>
<<set _ok to true>>
You hurl burning oil across the cavern floor. The fungus screams, a sound like wet paper tearing, and the spore clouds thin.
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $foeHp to 8 - ($hintSpore ? 2 : 0)>>
You find the weak point: the spores thin in the moving air, and the infected creatures move slowly. When they turn on you, they are already faltering.
<<else>>
<<set $foeHp to 13 - ($hintSpore ? 2 : 0)>>
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 4))>>
Spores burst around you and you choke, losing a few Stamina. The infected turn as one.
<</if>>

<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Sporebound Wanderers", hp:$foeHp, guard:0, pool:3, dmg:1, loot:8, win:"RiftLairWin"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: RiftLedger
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftLedger">><<set $lair to "ledger">>
A palisade of sharpened logs seals a cave mouth, red banners snapping above it. This is the camp of the Crimson Ledger, deserters and sellswords who broke their contracts and now tax the ravine. Their captain, Harl Vess, lounges on a barrel, a black sigil stone hanging from his belt like a trophy.

"Toll's five gold," he calls. "Or a good reason."

<<link "Bargain with him (Persuasion)">><<set $lairMethod to "Persuasion">><<goto "RiftLedgerResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Stare him down (Intimidation)">><<set $lairMethod to "Intimidation">><<goto "RiftLedgerResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Slip in after dark and steal the sigil (Stealth)">><<set $lairMethod to "Stealth">><<goto "RiftLedgerResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Refuse the toll and draw steel">><<set $lairMethod to "Fight">><<goto "RiftLedgerResolve">><</link>>
<<talklink "vess" "Talk with Harl Vess">>

:: RiftLedgerResolve
<<if $lairMethod is "Persuasion">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 3 - (($hintLedger ? 1 : 0) + ($vessWants ? 1 : 0)))>><<chk "pre" "Persuasion" _n>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Intimidation">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 2 - ($vessWants ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "pre" "Intimidation" _n>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Stealth">>
<<chk "fin" "Stealth" 2>>
<<else>>
<<set _ok to false>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<if $lairMethod is "Persuasion">>
Vess laughs and tosses you the stone. "The Ledger's contract was with the keep, and the keep never paid. Tell Marrow we'll go quietly, for a fair price." His company files out of the cave.
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Intimidation">>
Your stare lands like a hammer. Vess's grin dies. "Fine. Take your rock. The Ledger's leaving." His people pack up in sullen silence.
<<else>>
You slip between sentries, lift the sigil from Vess's belt as he snores, and vanish into the dark before anyone wakes.
<</if>>

<<if $lairMethod isnot "Stealth">>
<<joinlink "vess" "Offer Vess a paid contract with you" "RiftLairWin">>
<</if>>
[[Take the sigil|RiftLairWin]]
<<else>>
<<if $lairMethod isnot "Fight">>Your plan goes wrong. Vess's grin sours.<</if>>
"Then it's steel." The Ledger draws weapons.

<<link "Fight the Crimson Ledger!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Ledger Captain Harl Vess", hp:20, guard:2, pool:5, dmg:2, loot:14, win:"RiftLairWin"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: RiftSilk
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftSilk">><<set $lair to "silk">>
A cave hung floor to ceiling with pale silk. Cocooned shapes, cattle and one soldier's gauntlet, dangle from the webs. A dry, clicking sound comes from the dark. Half-buried in the nest, a black sigil stone gleams.

<<link "Read the web patterns for weak strands (Perception)">><<set $lairMethod to "Perception">><<goto "RiftSilkResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Hack a path with brute force (Athletics)">><<set $lairMethod to "Athletics">><<goto "RiftSilkResolve">><</link>>
<<if $lantern>><<link "Burn the webs with lantern oil">><<set $lairMethod to "Fire">><<goto "RiftSilkResolve">><</link>><</if>>

:: RiftSilkResolve
<<if $lairMethod is "Perception">>
<<chk "wit" "Perception" 2>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Athletics">>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 2>>
<<else>>
<<set _ok to true>>
Flame races along the silk, and the cave fills with smoke and clicking shrieks.
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $foeHp to 10 - ($hintSilk ? 2 : 0)>>
You cut the anchor strands and drop the nest's canopy. The Silk-Weaver scuttles out half-tangled.
<<else>>
<<set $foeHp to 16 - ($hintSilk ? 2 : 0)>>
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 4))>>
You blunder into the sticky lines and lose a few Stamina tearing free. The Silk-Weaver drops from the ceiling.
<</if>>
<<if $antitoxin>>Your antitoxin vial should dull its venom.<</if>>

<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Silk-Weaver", hp:$foeHp, guard:1, pool:5, dmg:($antitoxin ? 2 : 3), loot:10, win:"RiftLairWin"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: RiftCistern
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftCistern">><<set $lair to "cistern">>
Stairs of slick stone descend into a flooded cistern. Candles float on the black water, and on a rotting throne of driftwood sits Marga Crow, an old hag with river-weed hair and pearl-white eyes. A black sigil hangs in her necklace of bones.

"A visitor. Come, come. Everything has a price."

<<if $gold gte 10>><<link "Pay her 10 crowns">><<set $gold -= 10>><<set $lairMethod to "Pay">><<goto "RiftCisternResolve">><</link>><</if>>
<<link "Haggle with her (Persuasion)">><<set $lairMethod to "Persuasion">><<goto "RiftCisternResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Threaten her (Intimidation)">><<set $lairMethod to "Intimidation">><<goto "RiftCisternResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Attack the hag">><<set $lairMethod to "Fight">><<goto "RiftCisternResolve">><</link>>
<<talklink "marga" "Talk with Marga Crow">>

:: RiftCisternResolve
<<if $lairMethod is "Pay">>
<<set _ok to true>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Persuasion">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 3 - ($hintCistern ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "pre" "Persuasion" _n>>
<<elseif $lairMethod is "Intimidation">>
<<set _n to Math.max(1, 3 - ($hintCistern ? 1 : 0))>><<chk "pre" "Intimidation" _n>>
<<else>>
<<set _ok to false>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
Marga Crow cackles and unclasps the sigil from her necklace. "A fair trade. Take it, and take this too, dearie, for being polite." She presses a vial into your hand.
<<set $potions++>>
You gain a healing draught.

[[Take the sigil|RiftLairWin]]
<<else>>
<<if $lairMethod isnot "Fight">>Marga Crow's smile stretches too wide. "Rude."<</if>>
The candles gutter and the water rises around her. She rises, dripping.

<<link "Fight the Cistern Hag!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Cistern Hag", hp:20, guard:1, pool:5, dmg:2, loot:15, win:"RiftLairWin"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: RiftLairWin
<<if $lair is "spore">>
In the heart of the grotto you find a black sigil stone wrapped in fungal threads. As you lift it, the glow fades, and the spore-cursed wanderers slump gently to the floor, blinking, alive, and themselves again.
<<elseif $lair is "ledger">>
The Crimson Ledger's camp is yours. Vess's black sigil stone is in your hand.
<<elseif $lair is "silk">>
You cut the sigil stone from the Silk-Weaver's nest. The dry clicking in the dark has stopped.
<<else>>
The Brine Cistern falls quiet. The sigil is yours.
<</if>>

<<set $rift[$lair] to true>>
<<set $sigils++>>
<<run setup.rank()>>
<<set $gold += 12>>
You gain 12 crowns, a sigil stone (<<= $sigils>>/4), and grow more seasoned. <b>Rank <<= $rank>></b>: +3 max Stamina<<if $rank % 2 is 0>>, +1 attack die<</if>>.

<<if $sigils gte 3>>The sigils in your pack thrum in unison. The vault at the ravine's end can be opened.<</if>>

[[Return to the Rift|RiftRavine]]

:: RiftVault
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftVault">>
The sigils slot into the ash-black door one by one, and it swings inward on a breath of warm, sulfurous air.

Beyond lies a great hall of burnt stone. At its center, on a dais of cinders, burns the Ember Idol: a twisted iron brazier taller than a man, wreathed in soot-black flame. Around it, monsters from every lair in the Rift crouch and whisper, and before it kneels a priest in charred vestments.

"The keep's old chaplain," he says without turning. "Kessrick. Once I tended the dawn lamp. Now I feed the ember, and the ember feeds the Rift. It promised me the dark would never take my flock again."

<<if $sigils lt 4>><span class="dim">A fourth sigil socket in the door stands empty. The idol's hold is stronger for it.</span><</if>>

<<link "Speak to him (Persuasion)">><<goto "RiftVaultParley">><</link>>
<<if not $idolCracked>>
<<link "Sabotage the idol with Occult">><<set $lairMethod to "Occult">><<goto "RiftVaultSabotage">><</link>>
<<link "Sabotage the idol with Religion">><<set $lairMethod to "Religion">><<goto "RiftVaultSabotage">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The idol's flame gutters, cracked.</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Attack Kessrick!">><<goto "RiftVaultFight">><</link>>
<<talklink "kessrick" "Speak with Kessrick">>

:: RiftVaultParley
<<if $sigils gte 4>><<set _dc to 2>><<else>><<set _dc to 3>><</if>>
<<if $kessrickLore>><<set _dc to Math.max(1, _dc - 1)>><</if>>
<<chk "pre" "Persuasion" _dc>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $vaultPeace to true>>
You speak of the dawn lamp he once tended, and the flock that trusted him. Kessrick's shoulders shake. "It never promised light. Only ash." He rises, hands trembling, and lays his palm on the idol. The flame gutters, and dies.

[[Continue|RiftEnd]]
<<else>>
Kessrick shakes his head. "Too late. The ember has me." The idol roars, and the monsters rise.

[[Defend yourself!|RiftVaultFight]]
<</if>>

:: RiftVaultSabotage
<<if $lairMethod is "Occult">><<chk "wit" "Occult" 2>><<else>><<chk "wit" "Religion" 2>><</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $idolCracked to true>>
You find the idol's binding, a knot of ember and stolen prayer, and pull it loose. The black flame flares and shrinks, and Kessrick cries out as if struck.

[[Return|RiftVault]]
<<else>>
<<run setup.hurt(random(1, 6))>>
Hot ash blasts across your face, and you lose a few Stamina as Kessrick rises to face you.

[[Fight!|RiftVaultFight]]
<</if>>

:: RiftVaultFight
<<set $checkpoint to "RiftVault">>
<<set $bossDef to {name:"Ash-Priest Kessrick", hp:32, guard:2, pool:6, dmg:3, loot:0, win:"RiftEnd"}>>
<<set $bossDef.hp to Math.max(16, 32 - 3 * $sigils - ($idolCracked ? 5 : 0))>>
<<set $bossDef.pool to 6 - Math.floor($sigils / 2)>>

Kessrick lifts a hand and the Ember Idol answers, spilling black fire along the floor.

<<if $idolCracked>>The cracked idol gutters, and Kessrick looks weakened.<</if>>
<<if $sigils gte 3>>The sigils in your pack pulse, and something in the flame flinches.<</if>>

<<link "Fight the Ash-Priest!">><<run setup.startFight($bossDef)>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: RiftEnd
<<if $vaultPeace>>
The Ember Idol cools, cracks, and crumbles into ordinary soot. Across the Rift, the glowing caves dim, the chanting stops, and the monsters slink back into the hills, unbound.
<<else>>
Kessrick collapses beside the Ember Idol. The black flame gutters and dies, and the idol crumbles into ordinary soot. Across the Rift, the glowing caves dim, the chanting stops, and the monsters slink back into the hills, unbound.
<</if>>

You return to Thornwatch Keep as dawn breaks. Warden-Captain Isolde Marrow meets you at the gate and lets out a long breath.

"The wards are quiet. The patrols are already riding out." She counts out a heavy purse.
<<set $gold += 100>>
You gain 100 crowns.

The keep's guards raise their spears in salute as you pass. The Weeping Rift is only a ravine again, and <<= $name>> is the name they will tell around the fires.

<<for _be range setup.banterAll("end")>><p><i><<= _be>></i></p><</for>>
<h2>The End</h2>
<p><em><<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>>, Rank <<= $rank>>. Stamina <<= $hp>>/<<= $maxhp>>, <<= $gold>> crowns.</em></p>

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>


:: DeepIntro
Orrow's Rest is a hillside village of slate roofs and shuttered windows. For three generations its silver mine, Orrow's Deep, kept every lamp in the valley burning. Three weeks ago, the mine's lamps went out.

Mine-Warden Ilse Varn meets you at the winch house, a soot-stained woman gripping a lantern she never sets down. "The night crew stopped answering the signal-bells. The two who crawled out couldn't say what they saw. They just kept asking whether I'd blown out the lamps."

She glances at the black mouth of the shaft. "Light is life down there. Every step costs it. Find out what's wrong, and seal it if you can."

<<run setup.startDeep()>>

[[Prepare at the mine-head|DeepSurface]]

:: DeepSurface
<<set $crawling to false>>
Orrow's Rest crouches around the mine-head: a winch house, a bunkhouse, a dozen shuttered cottages. Warden Varn watches from the doorway.

<b>Down there, four things matter:</b>
* <b>Light.</b> Every step into the Deep burns 1 Light (nightsight stretches it). At 0, the dark feeds your Dread.
* <b>Dread</b>, from 0 to 10. At 3 you are Shaken (-1 die on everything), at 6 Haunted (-2 dice), and at 10 you break and flee.
* <b>Provisions.</b> You need 1 to make camp. Camping restores Stamina, Sparks and eases Dread, but it stirs the Deep.
* <b>The Stirring.</b> Every step and every rest stirs the Deep. When it fills, something hunts you.

You have <<= $gold>> crowns. Light <<= $light>>/12, oil flasks <<= $flasks>> (each refills 6 Light), Provisions <<= $prov>>, holy salt <<= $salt>> (each scatters 2 Dread), healing draughts <<= $potions>>.

<div class="actions">
<<if $gold gte 3>><<link "Oil flask (3 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 3>><<set $flasks++>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Oil flask: 3 crowns</span><</if>>
<<if $gold gte 2>><<link "Provisions (2 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 2>><<set $prov++>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Provisions: 2 crowns</span><</if>>
<<set _sp to ($saltDeal ? 3 : 5)>><<if $gold gte _sp>><<link `"Holy salt (" + _sp + " crowns)"`>><<set $gold -= _sp>><<set $salt++>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Holy salt: <<= _sp>> crowns</span><</if>>
<<if $gold gte 8>><<link "Healing draught (8 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 8>><<set $potions++>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Healing draught: 8 crowns</span><</if>>
<<if $flasks gt 0 and $light lt 12>><<link "Refill your lantern (+6 Light)">><<run setup.useFlask()>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><</if>>
<<if $gold gte 3>><<link "Rest in the bunkhouse (3 crowns)">><<set $gold -= 3>><<run setup.rest()>><<run setup.easeDread(3)>><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Bunkhouse bed: 3 crowns</span><</if>>
</div>

<<link "Descend into the Adit">><<set $checkpoint to "DeepAdit">><<goto "DeepAdit">><</link>>
<<talklink "varn" "Talk with Warden Varn">>
<<talklink "dorrin" "Talk with old Dorrin">>
<<recruitlink "deep">>
<<partylink>>

:: DeepAdit
<<set $crawling to true>><<set $depth to 1>>
The Adit is the mouth of the Deep: a timbered tunnel sloping into darkness, lantern hooks along both walls, every one empty. The air tastes of cold metal and old breath. A signal-bell hangs by the entrance, its clapper wrapped in cloth.

<div class="actions">
<<camplink>>
<<link "Climb back to Orrow's Rest">><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>>
<<move "DeepCarts" "Follow the cart rails (Cart Tunnel)">>
<<move "DeepBunk" "Take the side passage (Bunkhouse)">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepCarts
<<set $depth to 1>>
Rusted ore carts stand abandoned on the rails, their loads long since spilled. A faint murmur drifts down the tunnel, too soft to make out, like many voices speaking in the next room.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.carts>><<link "Search the carts">><<goto "DeepCartsSearch">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">You have searched the carts.</span><</if>>
<<if not $seen.whisper>><<link "Listen to the murmuring">><<goto "DeepCartsListen">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">The murmuring goes on.</span><</if>>
<<move "DeepAdit" "Back to the Adit">>
<<move "DeepShaft" "Go on to the collapsed shaft">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepCartsSearch
<<set $seen.carts to true>>
<<chk "wit" "Perception" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
Under a rotted tarp you find a miner's tin of hard biscuit, sealed and untouched. <b>+1 Provision.</b>
<<set $prov++>>
<<else>>
You lift the tarp, and a pale hand closes on your wrist. It is gone when you look again, but you can still feel the cold.
<<scare 2 1>>
<</if>>

[[Back|DeepCarts]]

:: DeepCartsListen
<<set $seen.whisper to true>>
<<chk "wit" "Discernment" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You hold your breath and sort the murmur into words. The same phrase, over and over: "Orrow Venn put out the lamps. Orrow Venn put out the lamps." A name, and maybe an order.
<<set $knowsName to true>>
<<else>>
The words slide through your ears like water. You catch only one, "dark," repeated until you feel your pulse in it.
<<run setup.gainDread(1)>>
<b>+1 Dread.</b>
<</if>>

[[Back|DeepCarts]]

:: DeepBunk
<<set $depth to 1>>
Rows of double bunks fill a long room. On every blanket lies a thin gray shape of dust in the outline of a sleeping person. Dozens of them, all facing the door.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.bunk>><<link "Step among the bunks">><<goto "DeepBunkLook">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">You have searched the bunks.</span><</if>>
<<camplink>>
<<move "DeepAdit" "Back to the Adit">>
<<move "DeepShaft" "Follow the drainage cut to the collapsed shaft">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepBunkLook
<<set $seen.bunk to true>>
As you step between the bunks, the dust shapes turn their heads to follow you. Nothing else moves.
<<scare 2 1>>
Whatever they were, they no longer need what lies beside them: a flask of lantern oil and a tin of provisions.
<<set $flasks++>><<set $prov++>>
<b>+1 oil flask, +1 Provision.</b>

[[Back|DeepBunk]]

:: DeepShaft
<<set $depth to 1>>
The tunnel ends in a rockfall that has half-sealed the way down. Beyond it, a crooked stair spirals into the dark.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.shaft>>
How will you get through?
<<link "Clamber over the rubble (Acrobatics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Acrobatics">><<goto "DeepShaftCross">><</link>>
<<link "Heave the stones aside (Athletics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Athletics">><<goto "DeepShaftCross">><</link>>
<<link "Hew a path with pick and patience (costs 2 Light)">><<set $deepMethod to "Hew">><<goto "DeepShaftCross">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">You have made the way passable.</span>
<<move "DeepLanding" "Descend the winding stair (Lower Landing)">>
<</if>>
<<move "DeepCarts" "Back to the Cart Tunnel">>
<<move "DeepBunk" "Back to the Bunkhouse">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepShaftCross
<<set $seen.shaft to true>>
<<if $deepMethod is "Acrobatics">>
<<chk "fin" "Acrobatics" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You scramble over the shifting stones and drop to the far side without a sound.
<<else>>
The stones shift under your feet. You slide, scrape, and land hard, and a little lantern oil spills into the dark.
<<run setup.hurt(random(2, 4))>><<run setup.burn(1)>>
<b>You lose some Stamina and 1 Light.</b>
<</if>>
<<elseif $deepMethod is "Athletics">>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 3>>
<<if _ok>>
You heave the boulders aside one by one and open a gap wide enough for a person.
<<else>>
A boulder slips and thunders down the shaft. The echo runs on for a long time.
<<set $stir += 2>>
<b>The Deep stirs.</b>
<</if>>
<<else>>
You spend long minutes hewing a gap, your lantern burning down beside you.
<<run setup.burn(2)>>
<b>-2 Light.</b>
<</if>>

[[Onward|DeepShaft]]

:: DeepLanding
<<set $depth to 2>>
The stair ends at the Lower Landing: a rail junction where three tunnels meet. Water drips somewhere far off. The air is colder here, and the dark seems denser, as if your lantern were pushing against it.

<div class="actions">
<<move "DeepFlood" "Take the drowned tunnel (Flooded Gallery)">>
<<move "DeepAssay" "Take the lit-once tunnel (Assay Office)">>
<<move "DeepChapel" "Take the arched tunnel (Chapel of Lamps)">>
<<move "DeepShaft" "Climb back to the shaft">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepFlood
<<set $depth to 2>>
A long gallery drowned to the knee in black water. Something long and pale ripples just beneath the surface, keeping pace with your lantern.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.flood>>
<<link "Wade straight through (Athletics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Wade">><<goto "DeepFloodResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Creep along the ledge (Stealth)">><<set $deepMethod to "Ledge">><<goto "DeepFloodResolve">><</link>>
<<if $flasks gt 0>><<link "Throw a burning oil flask to draw it off (costs 1 flask)">><<set $deepMethod to "Flask">><<goto "DeepFloodResolve">><</link>><</if>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The water is still now.</span>
<<move "DeepEcho" "Go on to the Echo Hall">>
<</if>>
<<move "DeepLanding" "Back to the Landing">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepFloodResolve
<<set $seen.flood to true>>
<<if $deepMethod is "Wade">>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 2>>
<<elseif $deepMethod is "Ledge">>
<<chk "fin" "Stealth" 2>>
<<else>>
<<set $flasks-->>
<<set _ok to true>>
You hurl a flask of burning oil far down the gallery. The water boils away from the flames, and the pale shape tears after them.
<b>-1 oil flask.</b>
<</if>>

<<if _ok>>
You reach the far end unmolested.
<<if $deepMethod isnot "Flask">>Something glints in the shallows: a sealed flask of lantern oil, dropped by an earlier crew. <<set $flasks++>><b>+1 oil flask.</b><</if>>

[[Onward|DeepFlood]]
<<else>>
The water erupts. A Silt-stalker, long as a boat and pale as a drowned thing, surges up with too many jointed fingers.

<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Silt-stalker", hp:14, guard:1, pool:5, dmg:2, loot:0, win:"DeepFlood"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepAssay
<<set $depth to 2>>
An assayer's office: ledgers, scales, a leaning shelf of ore samples. A single strongbox is bolted to the floor. On the desk lies an open journal, its last pages torn.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $journal>><<link "Read the journal">><<goto "DeepAssayRead">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">You have read the journal.</span><</if>>
<<if not $chalk>>
<<link "Pick the strongbox lock (Pilfering)">><<set $deepMethod to "Pilfering">><<goto "DeepAssayBox">><</link>>
<<link "Force the strongbox (Athletics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Force">><<goto "DeepAssayBox">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The strongbox is open.</span>
<</if>>
<<move "DeepLanding" "Back to the Landing">>
<<move "DeepChapel" "Go through to the Chapel of Lamps">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepAssayRead
<<set $stir += 1>>
<<chk "wit" "Investigation" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $journal to true>>
The foreman's cramped hand fills the surviving pages: <i>"It is not a beast. It is an absence, and it eats light. The old wardens sealed it in the Heart Vault with chalk of ground bone-silver and a rite of flame: four measures of light burned as a closing, and a name spoken to bind it. The chalk is in the strongbox. Whatever you do, do not let the lamps go out."</i>

The rite needs the chalk and 4 Light to burn.
<<else>>
Half the pages are stained and unreadable. You lose time, and the dust stirs, trying.

[[Try again|DeepAssayRead]]
<</if>>

[[Back|DeepAssay]]

:: DeepAssayBox
<<if $deepMethod is "Pilfering">>
<<chk "fin" "Pilfering" 2>>
<<else>>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 3>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $chalk to true>>
Inside lies a leather pouch of pale, gritty chalk that gleams faintly in the lantern light. <b>You take the sealing chalk.</b>
<<else>>
The box resists, and something inside it clangs like a bell. The sound rolls down the tunnels.
<<set $stir += 2>>
<b>The Deep stirs.</b>

[[Try again|DeepAssayBox]]
<</if>>

[[Back|DeepAssay]]

:: DeepChapel
<<set $depth to 2>>
A small stone chapel, and everywhere in its walls are niches holding lamps: hundreds of them, all dark, all cold. But there is a memory of warmth here, and the darkness keeps its distance from the altar.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.tam>><<link "Speak to the huddled figure behind the altar">><<goto "DeepChapelTam">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">Tam Orrick sits by the altar, watching the door.</span><</if>>
<<if not $seen.votive>><<link "Light the last dry votive lamp">><<set $seen.votive to true>><<set $light to Math.min(12, $light + 2)>><<goto "DeepChapel">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">You have lit the votive.</span><</if>>
<<camplink>>
<<move "DeepLanding" "Back to the Landing">>
<<move "DeepAssay" "Go through to the Assay Office">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

<<if $seen.votive>>The votive burns steadily, and its flame is warm. <b>+2 Light.</b><</if>>

Camping here is safer: it stirs the Deep less and eases Dread more.
<<if $seen.tam>>
<<talklink "tam" "Talk with Tam">>
<<if $party.indexOf("tam") lt 0>><<joinlink "tam" "Ask Tam to come along" "DeepChapel">><<else>><span class="dim">Tam is with you.</span><</if>>
<</if>>
<<partylink>>

:: DeepChapelTam
Behind the altar crouches a thin young hauler, his lantern long dead, his eyes fixed on nothing. He flinches when your light touches him.

"Are you real?" he whispers. "Don't speak to it. It uses your voice."

<<link "Coax him out gently (Persuasion)">><<set $deepMethod to "Persuasion">><<goto "DeepChapelTamResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Tend his wounds (Medicine)">><<set $deepMethod to "Medicine">><<goto "DeepChapelTamResolve">><</link>>
[[Leave him be|DeepChapel]]

:: DeepChapelTamResolve
<<if $deepMethod is "Persuasion">>
<<chk "pre" "Persuasion" 2>>
<<else>>
<<chk "wit" "Medicine" 2>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $seen.tam to true>><<set $survivor to true>><<set $prov += 2>>
He lets out a shaking breath. "Tam. Tam Orrick. I've been living on candle-tallow." He presses his last two biscuit tins into your hands and grips your sleeve. "I'll stay here. But if you go down, hum when you're scared. It helps. It kept me from listening."
<b>+2 Provisions.</b> Tam's steadiness helps you keep your nerve: <b>+1 die on Resolve checks.</b>
<<else>>
He shies away and gasps, and the sound echoes down the tunnels.
<<set $stir += 2>>
<b>The Deep stirs.</b>

[[Try again|DeepChapelTam]]
<</if>>

[[Back|DeepChapel]]

:: DeepEcho
<<set $depth to 2>>
A vaulted hall of smooth stone that carries every sound. Your footsteps reach you a moment before you make them. Somewhere ahead, a voice says your name, and it is your own voice.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.echo>>
<<link "Answer the voice (Resolve)">><<set $deepMethod to "Answer">><<goto "DeepEchoResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Stop your ears and run (Athletics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Run">><<goto "DeepEchoResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Sing back to it (Performance)">><<set $deepMethod to "Sing">><<goto "DeepEchoResolve">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The hall is quiet, for now.</span>
<<move "DeepGate" "Go on to the Lampless Gate">>
<</if>>
<<move "DeepFlood" "Back through the Flooded Gallery">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepEchoResolve
<<set $seen.echo to true>>
<<if $deepMethod is "Answer">>
<<chk "pre" "Resolve" 3>>
<<if _ok>>
You answer, and the voice answers you. It speaks from inside your own certainty, and for a while you speak to yourself. When it falls quiet, it has left one true thing behind: <i>"Orrow Venn is what binds it."</i>
<<set $knowsName to true>>
<<else>>
The voice tells you things about yourself that you did not know you believed. You are still shaking when it stops.
<<run setup.gainDread(2)>>
<b>+2 Dread.</b>
<</if>>
<<elseif $deepMethod is "Run">>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You clamp your hands over your ears and sprint the length of the hall. The voice screams behind you, and you do not stop until it is gone.
<<else>>
You cannot run fast enough. The voice climbs inside your head and follows you the whole way.
<<run setup.gainDread(1)>>
<b>+1 Dread.</b>
<</if>>
<<else>>
<<chk "pre" "Performance" 2>>
<<if _ok>>
You sing, badly, but with conviction. The voice hesitates, then falls silent, and in an alcove where its echo was strongest you find a miner's silver cache. <b>+20 crowns.</b>
<<set $gold += 20>>
<<else>>
Your song comes out thin. The voice sings it back to you, wrong, in a chorus of voices you do not want to identify.
<<run setup.gainDread(1)>>
<b>+1 Dread.</b>
<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $dread gte 10>><<goto "DeepBroken">><</if>>

[[Onward|DeepEcho]]

:: DeepGate
<<set $depth to 3>>
The Lampless Gate: a wall of black iron doors hung with a thousand lanterns, each on its own chain, all cold. The floor is wet with something that is not water. Your lantern gutters as if breathing out. From the gaps between the lanterns, a wick of smoke rises and takes the shape of a miner.

<div class="actions">
<<if not $seen.gate>>
<<link "Slip past it in the dark (Stealth)">><<set $deepMethod to "Sneak">><<goto "DeepGateResolve">><</link>>
<<set _oc to ($gateHint ? 2 : 3)>><<if $light gte _oc>><<link `"Offer it light (burn " + _oc + " Light)"`>><<set $deepMethod to "Offer">><<goto "DeepGateResolve">><</link>><</if>>
<<link "Fight the Wick-Wraith">><<set $deepMethod to "Fight">><<goto "DeepGateResolve">><</link>>
<<else>>
<span class="dim">The iron doors stand open.</span>
<<move "DeepHeart" "Enter the Heart Vault">>
<</if>>
<<move "DeepEcho" "Back to the Echo Hall">>
<<packlink>>
</div>

The Deep is too close here to make camp.

:: DeepGateResolve
<<if $deepMethod is "Sneak">>
<<chk "fin" "Stealth" 3>>
<<if _ok>>
<<set $seen.gate to true>>
You slip along the wall, keeping your lantern shuttered, until the wraith turns away and forgets you.

[[Onward|DeepGate]]
<<else>>
The wraith turns. The hanging lanterns tremble.

<<set $seen.gate to true>>
<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Wick-Wraith", hp:18, guard:2, pool:5, dmg:3, loot:0, win:"DeepGate"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>
<<elseif $deepMethod is "Offer">>
<<set $seen.gate to true>>
<<set _oc to ($gateHint ? 2 : 3)>><<run setup.burn(_oc)>>
You lift your lantern and let the flame burn high. The wraith reaches for it, then recoils, howling, and unravels like a burning thread. <b>-<<= _oc>> Light.</b>

[[Onward|DeepGate]]
<<else>>
<<set $seen.gate to true>>
The Wick-Wraith drifts toward you, trailing smoke.

<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.startFight({name:"Wick-Wraith", hp:18, guard:2, pool:5, dmg:3, loot:0, win:"DeepGate"})>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepHeart
<<set $depth to 3>>
The Heart Vault is a round chamber where the mine's first silver vein once surfaced. The vein is gone. Where it ran, there is a stillness the shape of a man, tall as the vault, made of everything the lamps ever lost. Your lantern shrinks to a bead. All around the walls hang small pale lights on chains: one for every miner who did not come home.

The Lampless One does not move. It does not need to.

<<if $knowsName>>You know its binding name.<</if>>

<div class="actions">
<<if $journal and $chalk and $light gte 4>>
<<link "Draw the seal and speak the closing (Religion)">><<set $deepMethod to "Religion">><<goto "DeepHeartSeal">><</link>>
<<link "Weave the seal with the chalk (Occult)">><<set $deepMethod to "Occult">><<goto "DeepHeartSeal">><</link>>
<<elseif $journal and $chalk>>
<span class="dim">You know the rite, but you have less than 4 Light to burn for it.</span>
<</if>>
<<link "Improvise a ward against it (Occult, very hard)">><<goto "DeepHeartWard">><</link>>
<<link "Attack the Lampless One">><<goto "DeepHeartFight">><</link>>
<<link "Grab a slab of raw silver and run (Stealth or Athletics)">><<goto "DeepHeartRun">><</link>>
<<packlink>>
</div>

:: DeepHeartSeal
<<run setup.burn(4)>>
<<set _need to $knowsName ? 2 : 3>>
You spill the chalk in a ring, set your lantern's flame to it, and begin. <b>-4 Light.</b>
<<if $deepMethod is "Religion">>
<<chk "pre" "Religion" _need>>
<<else>>
<<chk "wit" "Occult" _need>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
The chalk ring flares. The Lampless One shudders and folds toward the ring, and the whole vault rings like a struck bell.

[[Close the seal|DeepEndSeal]]
<<else>>
The ring gutters and the seal cracks. The Lampless One turns toward you. The little lights on the walls go out, one by one.
<<run setup.gainDread(2)>><<run setup.hurt(4)>>
<b>+2 Dread. You lose some Stamina.</b>
<<if $dread gte 10>><<goto "DeepBroken">><</if>>

<<link "Fight!">><<goto "DeepHeartFight">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepHeartWard
<<chk "wit" "Occult" 4>>
<<if _ok>>
You scrawl a ward in soot on the floor and speak the only binding words you can think of. It shouldn't work. It does.

[[Close the ward|DeepEndSeal]]
<<else>>
The ward fizzles. The Lampless One leans toward you.

<<link "Fight!">><<goto "DeepHeartFight">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepHeartFight
The more light you carry, the weaker it is.
<<set $foe to {name:"The Lampless One", hp:30, guard:2, pool:6, dmg:3, loot:0, win:"DeepEndDestroy"}>>
<<if $light lte 0>><<set $foe.pool to 7>>Your lantern is dead, and the Lampless One is stronger for it.<<elseif $light gte 4>><<set $foe.pool to 5>>Your lantern burns bright, and the Lampless One flinches from it.<</if>>

<<link "Stand and fight!">><<run setup.gainDread(1)>><<run setup.startFight($foe)>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>

:: DeepHeartRun
The vault's walls are lined with raw silver, more than a village could spend in a lifetime. The Lampless One does not stir. It is waiting to see what you will do.

<<link "Slip out with a slab (Stealth)">><<set $deepMethod to "Stealth">><<goto "DeepHeartRunResolve">><</link>>
<<link "Grab what you can and bolt (Athletics)">><<set $deepMethod to "Athletics">><<goto "DeepHeartRunResolve">><</link>>

:: DeepHeartRunResolve
<<if $deepMethod is "Stealth">>
<<chk "fin" "Stealth" 3>>
<<else>>
<<chk "vig" "Athletics" 3>>
<</if>>
<<if _ok>>
You are through the iron doors before the Lampless One turns its head.

[[Run for the surface|DeepEndGreed]]
<<else>>
Silver clatters, and the little lights go out.

<<set $foe to {name:"The Lampless One", hp:30, guard:2, pool:7, dmg:3, loot:0, win:"DeepEndDestroy"}>>
<<link "Fight!">><<run setup.gainDread(1)>><<run setup.startFight($foe)>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepEndSeal
The chalk ring blazes white, and the Lampless One folds inward like a page turning. In the silence after, the pale lights on the walls flare, one by one, and drift loose from their chains. They gather around you, warm and glad, and lead the way up.

At the mine-head, Warden Varn is already at the winch. Behind you, the shaft's lanterns are lighting themselves, row by row.
<<set $gold += 60>>
She counts out 60 crowns. "The Deep is quiet. You've given us back our light."

<<for _be range setup.banterAll("end")>><p><i><<= _be>></i></p><</for>>
<h2>The End</h2>
<p><em><<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>>. <<= $moves>> steps taken. Dread <<= $dread>>/10, Light <<= $light>>, <<= $gold>> crowns.</em></p>

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: DeepEndDestroy
The Lampless One tears apart in a rush of dark that pours out of the vault and up the shaft like a thousand bats. Then it is gone, and the little lights on the walls rise off their chains and go dim, one by one, at last at rest.

You climb out of the Deep on a single lantern flame, blinking in the dawn. Warden Varn is at the winch.
<<set $gold += 60>>
"It's gone. Whatever you did down there, it's gone." She presses 60 crowns into your hand and does not ask how you did it.

<<for _be range setup.banterAll("end")>><p><i><<= _be>></i></p><</for>>
<h2>The End</h2>
<p><em><<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>>. <<= $moves>> steps taken. Dread <<= $dread>>/10, Light <<= $light>>, <<= $gold>> crowns.</em></p>

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: DeepEndGreed
You reach the surface with a slab of raw silver on your shoulder and the dark at your back. It does not follow you out. It does not need to.

<<set $gold += 80>>
The silver sells for 80 crowns in the next town. The Deep stays sealed only by distance. Some nights, in your dreams, the lamps go out one by one.

<<for _be range setup.banterAll("end")>><p><i><<= _be>></i></p><</for>>
<h2>The End</h2>
<p><em><<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>>. <<= $moves>> steps taken. Dread <<= $dread>>/10, Light <<= $light>>, <<= $gold>> crowns.</em></p>

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: DeepPack
<h2>Your pack</h2>
Light <<= $light>>/12 &middot; Oil flasks <<= $flasks>> &middot; Provisions <<= $prov>> &middot; Holy salt <<= $salt>> &middot; Draughts <<= $potions>>

Dread <<= $dread>>/10: <<if $dread gte 6>>Haunted (-2 dice on everything)<<elseif $dread gte 3>>Shaken (-1 die on everything)<<else>>Steady<</if>>

<<if $journal>>You know the closing rite needs the chalk and 4 Light.<</if>>

<div class="actions">
<<if $flasks gt 0 and $light lt 12>><<link "Refill lantern (+6 Light)">><<run setup.useFlask()>><<goto "DeepPack">><</link>><</if>>
<<if $salt gt 0 and $dread gt 0>><<link "Scatter holy salt (-2 Dread)">><<run setup.useSalt()>><<goto "DeepPack">><</link>><</if>>
<<if $potions gt 0 and $hp lt $maxhp>><<link "Drink a healing draught">><<run setup.useDraught()>><<goto "DeepPack">><</link>><</if>>
</div>

<<link "Close your pack">><<goto $packFrom>><</link>>
<<partylink>>

:: DeepCamp
<<set $checkpoint to $campAt>>
<<if $campAt is "DeepChapel">>
You settle among the cold lamps. For a little while, the dark keeps its distance.
<<else>>
You wedge a bedroll against the wall, keep the lantern low, and try not to listen. Sleep comes in pieces.
<</if>>

You recover Stamina and Sparks, and some Dread lifts. <b>-<<= $lastCampCost>> Provision<<= $lastCampCost > 1 ? "s" : "">>.</b> The Deep stirs.

<<link "Break camp">><<goto $campAt>><</link>>
<<if $party.length>><<partylink>> (companions can talk once per rest)<</if>>

:: DeepHunt
<<set $hunt to false>>
<<run setup.gainDread(1)>>
<<if $dread gte 10>>
<<goto "DeepBroken">>
<<else>>
The Deep has noticed you. The lantern flame bows away from something you cannot see, and the temperature drops. <b>+1 Dread.</b>
<<if $depth is 1>>
<<set $foe to {name:"Skulking Dark", hp:10, guard:1, pool:4, dmg:2, loot:0, win:$huntDest}>>
A shape made of shadow peels itself off the wall.
<<elseif $depth is 2>>
<<set $foe to {name:"Hollow Miner", hp:14, guard:1, pool:5, dmg:2, loot:0, win:$huntDest}>>
A figure in a miner's coat steps into the light. There is nothing under its hat.
<<else>>
<<set $foe to {name:"Lampless Thing", hp:18, guard:2, pool:5, dmg:3, loot:0, win:$huntDest}>>
A tall shape unfolds from the dark, and the light in your lantern trembles toward it.
<</if>>

<<link "Stand and fight!">><<run setup.startFight($foe)>><<goto "Combat">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: DeepBroken
<<set $crawling to false>><<set $dread to 6>><<set $hunt to false>><<set $stir to 0>><<set $nextHunt to 6>>
<<run setup.breakParty()>><<set $prov to Math.max(0, $prov - 1)>><<set $checkpoint to "DeepAdit">>
Your nerve goes. You do not remember the climb. You remember the dark on your heels, and the crawl through the Adit's mouth into the dawn, and Warden Varn's hands on your shoulders as she drags you clear.

Whatever you did not finish is still down there. Your progress is not lost, but a bit of your supplies and your sleep are.

<b>-1 Provision. Dread settles at 6.</b>
<<if $leftNames.length>><p><i><<= $leftNames.join(" and ")>> could not take it, and left in the night.</i></p><</if>>

<<link "Recover at the mine-head">><<goto "DeepSurface">><</link>>


:: Talk
<<set _n to setup.npcs[$talkNpc]>>
<h2><<= _n.name>></h2>
<em><<= _n.title>></em>

<<= _n.greet>>

<<for _t range _n.topics>>
<<if not _t.req or _t.req()>>
<<capture _t>>
<<link `_t.label`>><<run setup.talkTopic($talkNpc, _t.id)>><<goto "TalkTopic">><</link>>
<</capture>>
<br>
<</if>>
<</for>>

<<link "Finish talking">><<goto $talkBack>><</link>>

:: TalkTopic
<<set _n to setup.npcs[$talkNpc]>>
<b><<= _n.name>></b>
<<for _p range $topicText>><p><<= _p>></p><</for>>
<<if $topicNote>><div class="check pass"><<= $topicNote>></div><</if>>

<<link "Ask something else">><<goto "Talk">><</link>>
<<link "Finish talking">><<goto $talkBack>><</link>>

:: Recruit
<h2>The wanderers' table</h2>
<<if $recruitHub is "bell">>
In a corner of the Gilded Heron, a few travelers sit apart from the drinkers, eating slowly, watching the room. They look like people who have been on the road a long time and are ready for a reason to stay on it.
<<elseif $recruitHub is "rift">>
Along the back wall of the Broken Shield, a handful of hard-eyed sellswords and wanderers nurse cheap drinks. They have the look of people who follow the coin, or the story.
<<else>>
On the bunkhouse steps at Orrow's Rest, a few travelers wait out the last of the daylight, not quite ready to go down the shaft and not quite willing to leave.
<</if>>

Your party: <<= $party.length>>/2 companions. You have <<= $gold>> crowns.

<<for _id range setup.hubRoster[$recruitHub]>>
<<if $party.indexOf(_id) lt 0>>
<<capture _id>>
<div class="opt"><b><<= setup.companions[_id].name>></b>, <<= setup.companions[_id].title>><br><small><<= setup.companions[_id].role>>: <<= setup.companions[_id].roleText>> Trained: <<= setup.companions[_id].skills.join(", ")>>. Fee: <<= setup.companions[_id].fee>> crowns.</small><br><i><<= setup.companions[_id].pitch[0]>></i><br>
<<if $party.length lt 2 and $gold gte setup.companions[_id].fee>><<link `"Hire " + setup.companions[_id].short + " (" + setup.companions[_id].fee + " crowns)"`>><<run setup.recruit(_id)>><<goto "Recruit">><</link>><<else>><span class="dim">You cannot hire <<= setup.companions[_id].short>> right now (party full or not enough crowns).</span><</if>></div>
<</capture>>
<</if>>
<</for>>

<<link "Leave the table">><<goto $recruitBack>><</link>>

:: Party
<h2>Your party</h2>
<<= $name>>, <<= $race>> <<= $class>> (you).

<<if $party.length is 0>>You travel alone. There are people who might travel with you, if you find them.<</if>>
<<for _id range $party>>
<<capture _id>>
<div class="opt"><b><<= setup.companions[_id].name>></b>, <<= setup.companions[_id].title>><br>
<small><<= setup.companions[_id].role>>: <<= setup.cstat(_id).roleText>> Trained: <<= setup.companions[_id].skills.join(", ")>>.</small><br>
Trust: <<= "♥".repeat($trust[_id] || 0) + "♡".repeat(3 - ($trust[_id] || 0))>><br>
<<link "Talk">><<run setup.partyTalk(_id)>><<goto "PartyTalk">><</link>>
<<link "Send away">><<run setup.dismiss(_id)>><<goto "Party">><</link>>
</div>
<</capture>>
<</for>>

<span class="dim">Companions can talk once per rest. Each talk deepens Trust, up to 3. Two companions fit in your party. More companions make foes tougher and camps cost an extra Provision.</span>

<<link "Back">><<goto $partyBack>><</link>>

:: PartyTalk
<<set _c to setup.companions[$partyTalkId]>>
<h2><<= _c.name>></h2>
<<for _p range $partyTalkText>><p><<= _p>></p><</for>>
<<if $partyTalkNote>><div class="check pass"><<= $partyTalkNote>></div><</if>>

[[Back to your party|Party]]

:: PartyJoin
<p><<= $joinMsg>></p>

<<link "Continue">><<goto $joinBack>><</link>>
